{
  "suite": "hierarchy",
  "level": 2,
  "about": "Outlines: an object inside another object, in order. The failure this suite exists to prevent is a tree arriving as a list with no sign that it ever was one.",
  "requires": {
    "features": [
      "hierarchy"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "hierarchy/an-outline-is-parents-and-positions",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "outline",
      "given": {
        "objects": [
          {
            "id": "o_a",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a"
            },
            "position": "a0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_b",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_b"
            },
            "position": "a1"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a2",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a2"
            },
            "parent": "o_a",
            "position": "b1"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a1",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a1"
            },
            "parent": "o_a",
            "position": "b0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a3",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a3"
            },
            "parent": "o_a",
            "position": "b2"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a2x",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a2x"
            },
            "parent": "o_a2",
            "position": "c0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "id": "o_a",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "o_a1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "id": "o_a2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "o_a2x",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "o_a3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "o_b",
          "children": []
        }
      ],
      "why": "The whole of it: an object names the object it is inside and its place among that object's children. No `children` array anywhere \u2014 a parent pointer cannot disagree with itself, and a list of children on the parent can disagree with the parents on the children."
    },
    {
      "id": "hierarchy/siblings-sort-byte-wise",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "outline",
      "given": {
        "objects": [
          {
            "id": "o_r",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_r"
            },
            "position": "a0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_z",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_z"
            },
            "parent": "o_r",
            "position": "Zz"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_x",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_x"
            },
            "parent": "o_r",
            "position": "a0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_y",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_y"
            },
            "parent": "o_r",
            "position": "a0V"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "id": "o_r",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "o_z",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "id": "o_x",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "id": "o_y",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "why": "The same rule collection members follow, and the same failure if it is broken: under a language-aware collation 'Zz' sorts after 'a0' and the top of the outline is wrong. These tokens are compared, never parsed."
    },
    {
      "id": "hierarchy/a-missing-parent-is-a-root-for-now",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "outline",
      "given": {
        "objects": [
          {
            "id": "o_kid",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_kid"
            },
            "parent": "o_absent",
            "position": "a0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_top",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_top"
            },
            "position": "a1"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "id": "o_kid",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "o_top",
          "children": []
        }
      ],
      "why": "A `since` read is a delta and will routinely carry a child whose parent has not changed and is therefore not in the payload. Dropping it loses somebody's writing over a detail of transport; inventing a placeholder parent puts a node in their outline that they did not write. It stands at the root until the parent turns up."
    },
    {
      "id": "hierarchy/a-cycle-is-invalid",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "validate",
      "given": {
        "objects": [
          {
            "id": "o_1",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_1"
            },
            "parent": "o_2",
            "position": "a0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_2",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_2"
            },
            "parent": "o_1",
            "position": "a0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "valid": false,
        "errors": [
          {
            "code": "hierarchy.cycle"
          }
        ]
      },
      "why": "An object that is its own ancestor describes no document and hangs anything that walks it. Not a fidelity question and not something to cope with \u2014 a consumer that meets one has already been given a broken export, and the only useful thing to do is say so."
    },
    {
      "id": "hierarchy/self-parent-is-a-cycle-too",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "validate",
      "given": {
        "objects": [
          {
            "id": "o_1",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_1"
            },
            "parent": "o_1",
            "position": "a0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "valid": false,
        "errors": [
          {
            "code": "hierarchy.cycle"
          }
        ]
      },
      "why": "The one-node case, which a walker looking only for repeats two steps apart will miss."
    },
    {
      "id": "hierarchy/flattening-must-be-reported",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "import",
      "given": {
        "objects": [
          {
            "id": "o_a",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a"
            },
            "position": "a0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_b",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_b"
            },
            "position": "a1"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a2",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a2"
            },
            "parent": "o_a",
            "position": "b1"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a1",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a1"
            },
            "parent": "o_a",
            "position": "b0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a3",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a3"
            },
            "parent": "o_a",
            "position": "b2"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a2x",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a2x"
            },
            "parent": "o_a2",
            "position": "c0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "when": {
        "importInto": "a tool with no notion of containment"
      },
      "with": {
        "hierarchy": false
      },
      "simulated": true,
      "expect": {
        "fidelity": "reduced",
        "reports": [
          "hierarchy"
        ]
      },
      "why": "Importing an outline as a flat list is permitted, because refusing helps nobody. Doing it quietly is not: the nesting is what the document *was*, and a person who exported an outline and imported a list has lost the structure and been told nothing."
    },
    {
      "id": "hierarchy/a-flattener-still-gives-it-back",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "roundtrip",
      "given": {
        "objects": [
          {
            "id": "o_a",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a"
            },
            "position": "a0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_b",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_b"
            },
            "position": "a1"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a2",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a2"
            },
            "parent": "o_a",
            "position": "b1"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a1",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a1"
            },
            "parent": "o_a",
            "position": "b0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a3",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a3"
            },
            "parent": "o_a",
            "position": "b2"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_a2x",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_a2x"
            },
            "parent": "o_a2",
            "position": "c0"
          }
        ]
      },
      "when": {
        "importInto": "a tool with no notion of containment",
        "reexport": true
      },
      "with": {
        "hierarchy": false
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": {
          "objects": [
            {
              "id": "o_a2x",
              "parent": "o_a2",
              "position": "c0"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "why": "The round-trip rule, on the keys a flat tool has no use for. It may draw a list and must still hand back a tree, because the alternative is that opening somebody's outline in the wrong application destroys it."
    },
    {
      "id": "hierarchy/containment-is-not-membership",
      "level": 2,
      "op": "outline",
      "given": {
        "objects": [
          {
            "id": "o_p",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_p"
            },
            "position": "a0"
          },
          {
            "id": "o_c",
            "type": "t_note",
            "properties": {
              "title": "o_c"
            },
            "parent": "o_p",
            "position": "b5"
          }
        ],
        "collection": {
          "id": "c_1",
          "name": "A list",
          "members": [
            {
              "object": "o_c",
              "position": "a0"
            },
            {
              "object": "o_p",
              "position": "a1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "of": "envelope",
      "expect": [
        {
          "id": "o_p",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "o_c",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "why": "The same two objects, nested one way and listed the other, with a different position in each. A collection says what is in a list; a parent says what a thing is inside. Reading either as the other gives a document nobody wrote."
    }
  ]
}